 {"id":"fabro-6be6","title":"Platform: dedicated fabro host as production baseline (server + self-hosted Daytona stack)","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-12T11:15:49.473Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-12T11:15:49.473Z","description":"User direction (2026-09-12, merge session): fabro moves from the local WSL2 test environment to a dedicated host. The local instance stays as the test/dev loop.\n\nBaseline stack on the dedicated host:\n- fabro server (docker compose, storage volumes, secrets)\n- self-hosted Daytona (docker compose: server + DB + snapshot storage) as the provider-owned sandbox layer\n\nDecisions to make:\n- storage layout + backups for both stateful services\n- network topology (how the local test env reaches the remote instance; provider access from fabro to Daytona)\n- driver rev coupling: fabro pins sandbox-driver by rev; Daytona provider behavior advances with driver bumps — track per upstream merge\n- migration of existing environments (SQLite env store export/import) vs greenfield\n\nAcceptance:\n- dedicated host runs fabro + Daytona via compose with documented ops (upgrade, backup, restore)\n- at least one workflow run executes end to end against a Daytona sandbox on that host\n- local test loop unaffected","labels":["platform","daytona","deployment"]}
 {"id":"fabro-a0e5","title":"Multi-project run environments on Daytona (provider-owned image management)","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-12T11:15:49.566Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-12T11:15:49.566Z","description":"Future: several projects run in the autonomous fabro line (today: dogfooding only). Each project needs its own run images; image provisioning must scale without per-project operator builds.\n\nDirection (user decision 2026-09-12): provider-owned image management on self-hosted Daytona — Daytona builds Dockerfile->snapshot with content-hash caching, exactly the semantics the fork retired with the bollard autobuild (fabro-969f/72a0/3822). Fabro stays provider-neutral.\n\nImage definition format is OPEN (user: devcontainer.json was one idea, not a requirement). Candidates to evaluate through the pinned driver rev:\n- inline image.dockerfile in the environment (driver mapping exists upstream)\n- in-repo Dockerfile referenced by path (fabro resolves to inline content)\n- devcontainer.json (needs translation; driver contract has no devcontainer variant)\n- Daytona prebuilds / snapshot ids referenced by the environment\n\nProbe criteria (on the dedicated host, non-critical env first, e.g. mise):\n- image-as-config per env without manual rebuilds\n- run latency parity vs docker provider\n- memory/ops cost of the Daytona stack acceptable\n- the chosen image-definition format verified end-to-end through the driver\n\nInterim until the probe: docker provider + just run-images (deploy-time builds, label sh.fabro.toolchain.sha256).","labels":["daytona","sandbox","environments"]}
